}# Phase 9 optional end-to-end writer review packet

**Status:** NOT RUN. Optional under D046; no human result is claimed.

Use only rights-cleared screenplay material with the corpus/privacy rules in documents 28 and 34. The study is about workflow usefulness, not a universal screenplay score and not proof of audience response.

## Suggested comparison

For one real feature-screenplay concern, preserve the same base revision, note/concern text and protected strengths. Compare a normal human-only revision path with an agent-assisted Phase-9 session where the writer can see preflight, diagnosis evidence, strategy alternatives, candidate pages, exact diff, post-candidate revision packet and explicit accept/reject controls.

Evaluate separately whether: the diagnosis clarified the concern; reaction/cause/treatment stayed distinguishable; alternatives were meaningfully different in dramatic mechanism; the generated pages actually embodied their stated strategies; protected strengths survived; collateral/causal consequences were useful; resource information was understandable; the writer packet was usable without a bespoke GUI; and the writer still felt in control of canon.

Record disagreements, abstentions and non-findings. Do not ask reviewers for one total quality score or infer that acceptance means the model's diagnosis was objectively correct. If the study is skipped, retain `NOT RUN` as visible validation debt.{
