}# Phase 9 implementation matrix — Workshop Intelligence Integration

**Status:** `OFFLINE_IMPLEMENTED`. Runtime QC is pending. Phase 10 is not implemented.

| Product requirement | Phase-9 implementation | Offline evidence | Screenplay-writing usefulness |
|---|---|---|---|
| playbook diagnosis before substantial rewrites | `FountWorkshop.Writing.Intelligence` maps revision workflows onto installed `scene_doctor`, `sequence_momentum`, `character_trajectory`, and `setup_payoff` playbooks; `Writing.Preparation` runs this after the existing context/inspection path when an Observe provider is supplied | `phase_nine_intelligence_test.exs`; source-contract tests | A rewrite can start from source-grounded diagnosis rather than asking the generation model to diagnose and rewrite in one opaque step. |
| preserve generation-only hosts | Observe remains optional; missing analysis becomes explicit `status=not_run`, while `Session.services/1` still requires only Store + `Inference.Client` | Phase-9 source tests | Existing screenplay generation remains usable without forcing a new provider/runtime dependency. |
| provider-free resource preflight | `FountWorkshop.preflight/3` / `Session.preflight/3` validates the request and combines generation caps with `Fount.Intelligence.preflight_capability_playbook/4` without dispatch | focused test + source check | A caller can show likely generation/analysis work before spending provider calls. |
| note reaction/cause/treatment separation | Phase-9 note triage preserves raw note, reported reaction, suggested cause and suggested treatment as separate fields; free text is not promoted into an invented diagnosis/treatment | focused test | A writer's symptom report does not become a model-authored prescription by accident. |
| diagnosis → strategy → candidate lineage | writer packet IDs/diagnosis IDs/resource metadata attach to strategies and candidate provenance | bridge/strategy/generation/candidate source checks | Review can answer why a candidate exists and which diagnosis/strategy produced it. |
| causally distinct alternatives | strategy validation rejects exact duplicate premise/mechanism/change/consequence signatures in one generated set | Strategy source + source-contract test | “Three alternatives” cannot be literal causal duplicates with cosmetic wording changes. |
| analysis-guided generation context | compacted writer packet semantic sections are added to provider prompt context while full packet remains in saved provenance | `Writing.Context.prompt_data/2` + bridge | The generator can respond to diagnosis/protected strengths without flooding prompts with analysis plumbing. |
| pre/post candidate analysis | prewrite capability packet is stored in context/provenance; `Candidate.check/4` runs explicit base/candidate `revision_regression` when Phase-9 session context and Observe are supplied | Candidate bridge + focused/source tests | Review can compare what changed after real pages were generated, not just what the strategy promised. |
| protected-strength regression checks | Revision Intelligence protected-strength evidence is projected into advisory candidate checks | focused test | Writers see possible regressions without turning model interpretation into an automatic rejection rule. |
